COMPARISON WITH THE VALUES PRINTED IN Sec. 6.5
===========================================================================
  min |F(t_g)|, paper 0.01640...       computed 0.0164059726231506449728559925801532227775   (cores)
                                       computed 0.0028981930370156056829934707734133945166   (full sections)
  Gram lambda_min, paper 0.0375...     computed 0.0375896217904587160833584814961314315094   (eps-weighted)
                                       computed 0.0492735047360112464597667677650618984178   (unweighted)
  Gram det, paper 0.0249...            computed 0.0249347131811282750419050576626412787485   (eps-weighted)
                                       computed 0.0294593573487552215464171167261270584683   (unweighted)
  eq:indep constant, paper 0.19        computed 0.1938804316852495459270759030416734636059   (eps-weighted)
  grade-two lambda_min, paper 0.2054   computed 0.2054051461459432349256240690200706855493   (unweighted)
                                       computed 0.2054051461459432349256240690200706855493   (eps-weighted)

Sec. 6.5 quotes 0.01640... and 0.0375... / 0.0249... under two different
conventions, and both are reproduced above.

  0.01640... is the minimum over the six algebraic CORES.  Over the six full
  sections of eq:EKclosed the minimum is 0.00289..., attained at slot (1,1)
  and not at wp.  Sec. 6.1 declares the tables to be cores, so the number is
  right; the word 'sections' in Sec. 6.5 is what does not match it.

  0.0375... and 0.0249... are the EPS-WEIGHTED vectors, that is the
  class-invariant vectors eps(g)^{-(a+b)} e*_{a,b}(t_g) of eq:classinvwt,
  equivalently the r_{a,b} of eq:jetpackage, which differ from them by the
  positive scalar A^{-a} and so have the same normalised vectors.  The
  unweighted vectors give 0.0492... and 0.0294... instead.  eq:indep writes
  the hat over e*_{a,b}; the constant 0.19 belongs to the weighted vectors.

The conclusion that no nonzero constant-coefficient combination of the six
vanishes identically on D_E holds under either convention: both smallest
eigenvalues are bounded away from zero, and only the constant in eq:indep
changes, from 0.19 to 0.22.
